Title: Hermetic test fixtures in test_hook.sh and test_roundtrip.sh replicate outdated hook logic
Created: 2026-06-04
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-06-04T10:15Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context
Surfaced by the /verify gate on PR #268 (raid 219-224, ticket 0219).
0219 replaced the hardcoded `!= "main"` comparison in hookBody with
dynamic default-branch detection, and added a coherence guard that
byte-compares the installed hook against the integration.md snippet.
But tests/test_hook.sh and tests/test_roundtrip.sh carry independent
hand-rolled copies of the OLD `!= "main"` hook logic as hermetic
fixtures: they are not extracted from hookBody, so they still pass
and the new coherence guard does not cover them. They silently
diverge from the shipped hook behaviour.

## Actions
1. Decide per fixture: extract from hookBody (preferred, keeps them
   honest) or update the hand-rolled copy to the dynamic-detection
   form with a comment naming the divergence risk.
2. If extraction is feasible, route them through the same managed
   block used by the test_selfcoherence.sh guard (iv).

## Test
A grep for '"main"' (hardcoded literal in hook-shaped fixtures) over
tests/*.sh returns no hits outside the negative-control cases.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] test_hook.sh fixture matches shipped hookBody behaviour
- [ ] test_roundtrip.sh fixture matches shipped hookBody behaviour
- [ ] make check passes
